Description: log server for TOS - unified log platform for TerraMaster TOS (collect, audit, monitor, forward, receive)
 A unified log platform for TerraMaster TOS: audit retention, real-time monitoring,
 log forwarding to a remote log server, and acting as a standard syslog server that
 receives logs from switches/firewalls/other hosts.
 .
 Runs as a dedicated unprivileged user inside a hardened systemd sandbox. Runtime data
 is stored on a data volume (/Volume<N>/@apps/log-server-for-tos/data), never on the system partition.
 The bundled VictoriaLogs storage engine is built from upstream source with a public,
 bit-reproducible recipe. Standard syslog ports 514/6514 are used (requires
 AmbientCapabilities=CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE, which is the only capability requested).
 .
 "apt remove" keeps /Volume<N>/@apps/log-server-for-tos; "apt purge" deletes configuration but
 never touches user data or the shared folder.
